{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The route-deviation threshold in POL-RD-01 is not met on this trip's own trace, and the GPS artifact says so in terms: the derived deviation status is 'no deviation'. The measured excess is 0.11 km, or 4.400% of the 2.5 km optimal route, against gates of 0.8 km absolute and 20% that must BOTH be exceeded. POL-RD-01 provides that if either establishment test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The rider's case is therefore over at the first gate.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 requires the trace figure to govern over the rounded convenience copy on the trip_record, and I take the trace figure as it directs: trace_distance_km 2.61 km against optimal_distance_km 2.5 km. The point is in any event immaterial to the outcome, because the excess is 0.11 km on the trace and roughly 0.1 km on the rounded actual_distance_km of 2.6 km - an order of magnitude below the 0.8 km gate and a fifth of the 20% gate on either reading. There is no reading of this record on which the deviation gate opens.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Under POL-RD-08 the rider carries the initial burden, and limb (b) of that clause requires her to show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold. She has not: the excess she must prove is 4.4% and 0.11 km, well under both gates. The burden therefore never shifts to the driver at all, and the driver is not called upon to point to any exculpatory artifact. No traffic_advisory is needed to answer a defence that consists entirely of a failed numeric test, and the driver's answering statement that metered waiting time forms part of the fare is an explanation, not an invocation of POL-RD-03.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 and I say so expressly so that the point cannot be run against the driver: 145 fixes at a 10 s cadence across a 24-minute trip, coverage_pct 100.0, gaps empty, max_gap_sec 0.0 - no gap over 90 seconds, no jump over 500 m, no sustained interval above 30 seconds. None of limbs (a) to (c) is engaged, so the POL-RD-10(3) escalation route (impaired trace with no independent corroboration) is closed, and the excess figure may be relied on directly. The trace also identifies the same trip as the other artifacts: first_fix_at 18:31:40 matches trip_record.started_at, and last_fix_at 18:55:40 matches ended_at, so POL-RD-08(a) is satisfied and the POL-RD-10(4) timestamp-disagreement trigger does not fire.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The bundle's traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00529-01, has admissibility status MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, and I disclose that plainly: it carries no payload and can establish no fact; its only citable content is its own absence. That absence does not escalate this case. POL-RD-13(1) provides that where the asserting party names no evidence ID for an advisory the absence is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it, and no party here invokes POL-RD-03 on the driver's side - the driver's answer is that the threshold was never crossed, not that traffic excused a crossing. POL-RD-10(5) is therefore not triggered by this artifact, and no exculpatory clause has been invoked against a cited artifact that is missing from the pool.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00529-01", "EV-GPS-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-ADVIS-00529-01].admissibility.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-02's recomputation runs only 'where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01 and no exculpatory clause fully excuses it'. No deviation is established, so the recomputation is never reached, no recomputed_fare arises and no refund is available on the distance or time lines. The congestion the rider describes is priced by the meter itself and is itemised on the fare breakdown under rate card RC-SG-2026Q3-RYDETAXI: time_fare 6.72 and a waiting_time_fee of 3.08, against a total_charged of 16.35. Nothing in this policy makes metered time refundable in the absence of a deviation, and the rider's wider grievance - that the app was cheaper before electric vehicles - is not a ground any loaded clause provides for; I do not ask the tribunal to change the policy, only to apply it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.waiting_time_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "NO_ACTION is party-relative under POL-GEN-03: it means the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands - fare_breakdown.payment_status and refund_issued_sgd are left exactly as they are. This dispute is rider-filed, payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so NO_ACTION leaves the SGD 16.35 metered fare standing in full and the driver retains it. The contested SGD 5.40 is not returned, and nothing is netted against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the tribunal ran the POL-RD-06 check, no pattern could be established against this driver: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 250, and 0 divided by 250 is far below the 0.05 ratio that clause requires, while the count itself is below the threshold of 3. It follows that no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is open on this record. I rely on no other field of either profile: POL-GEN-01 confines rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, cancellation_rate, prior_deviation_flags, prior_no_show_flags and the rest to context, and I cite none of them as a ground.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own track corroborates slow movement in traffic rather than any detour: across 145 fixes the distinct speeds run continuously between 4.6 and 8.2 km/h, and the entire 2.61 km trace exceeds the 2.5 km optimal route by only 0.11 km. A driver who had taken another road to avoid or exploit congestion would show excess distance; this trace shows almost none. The single 100-second in-app call the rider complains of is recorded on the trip record as placed by the driver at 19:35:40, after the trip ended at 18:55:40, and whatever its tone it is not a fact from which a metered fare becomes refundable under any clause of this policy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

