    "explanation": "To both parties. This is a 2.6 km taxi trip, ION Orchard to Great World on 17 Sep 2026, charged at SGD 16.35 on rate card RC-SG-2026Q3-RYDETAXI. The charge stands: the evidence does not support a refund, and both money fields are empty.\n\nThe distance test fails on the trip's own record. The governing figure is the GPS trace's 2.61 km against the booked optimal of 2.5 km (POL-RD-01), an excess of 0.11 km, or 4.4%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess exceeds both 0.8 km and 20% of the optimal route; this excess fails both gates, so no deviation exists on this trip and the distance field decides nothing. Rider advocate's own second claim concedes exactly this, and the driver's answer on the same point is accepted: the trace figure governs over the rounded 2.6 km convenience copy, and neither reading opens the gate.\n\nThe rider's real complaint is the time billed — 24.0 metered minutes against a 9.0-minute optimal route — and the SGD 3.08 waiting-time line, with the driver's explanation that 'meter waiting time is part of the fare'. The frustration is understandable, but no loaded clause makes metered time or waiting time refundable where no route deviation is established. The POL-RD-02 recomputation runs only 'where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01 and no exculpatory clause fully excuses it'; it is therefore never reached, and the SGD 12.075 recomputed figure and the SGD 4.30 it would imply are not payable. The SGD 16.35 is base 3.80 + distance 1.95 + time 6.72 + waiting 3.08 + platform fee 0.80, which is what the meter produced, and the fare breakdown's own derived arithmetic matches that total.\n\nThe driver's traffic explanation needs no advisory behind it, because the driver was never called on to excuse anything: the rider's own trace shows no deviation, so the POL-RD-08 burden never shifted to the driver, and an uncited assertion carries no weight in any event. For completeness, the bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00529-01, is status MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. I name it and its weight as POL-GEN-02(3) requires, and I confirm the finding does not rest on it: its absence is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it (POL-RD-13(1)), so it neither excuses the driver nor escalates the case, and the trace at weight 1.0 alone disposes of the dispute.\n\nThe trace is not impaired. It carries 145 fixes at a 10 s cadence, coverage_pct 100.0, max_gap_sec 0.0, no jump over 500 m and no sustained interval over 30 s, so POL-RD-07(a)-(c) is not engaged and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation route is closed. The artifacts identify the same trip (TRP-00529 on all three; first_fix_at 18:31:40 matches trip_record.started_at, last_fix_at 18:55:40 matches ended_at), so POL-RD-08(a) is satisfied and no POL-RD-10(4) timestamp trigger fires.\n\nOn the profiles: the driver's POL-RD-06 figures are deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 250, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established — no FULL_REFUND uplift under limb (b) and no conduct referral under limb (c). The rider's deviation_claims_60d is 0, so no enhanced-corroboration gate under POL-RD-08 applies; that does not create a deviation either. No other profile field is used as a ground. Nothing shows a billing-integrity defect: no ERP gantry was charged (tolls 0.00, erp_gantries empty) and no airport surcharge was applied, so POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to correct and produces no referral. The driver's post-trip phone call is recorded (100 seconds, placed at 19:35:40, after the 18:55:40 end) and is not a fact any clause of this policy turns into a refund. The rider's wider point that the app was cheaper under an earlier fleet is a policy question, not a charge any loaded clause can unwind.\n\nBecause this is a rider-filed dispute, NO_ACTION leaves the fare as charged: payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 stand, and the contested SGD 5.40 is not returned. I have no doubt in this outcome and the escalation routes do not fire."
